    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e1b0603b-7c92-5a50-9971-57d25ef5739a" activityNameId="2e09666d-a556-50c2-9a09-b55ccf8efbed" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Section bar rolling, steel</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Section bar rolling, steel
As most other types of mills, section rolling mills are divided into roughing, intermediate and finish-ing stands, preceded by a descaling machine installed between the reheating furnace and the roughing mill. After cooling on the cooling bed, the bars are straightened on mechanical or hydraulic straightening machines and cut to length by saws as required;
Synonyms: profile; 
UUID: a36dd67e-350c-3400-9b1e-f0353d434a99
The module describes the rolling process of section bar. It includes 50% of the wire drawing process. Does not include the material being rolled
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average technique for EU. Because of the lack of data about the production process, it was approximated with the production process of wire drawing.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature and estimation 
Extrapolations: see technology
Uncertainty adjustments: The extrapolatin made for the description of the technology process and the fact that no data were available about the percentage of companies represented by the study citated are considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a36dd67e-350c-3400-9b1e-f0353d434a99.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
